		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=5065&amp;p=36776#p36776"><![CDATA[
<blockquote class="uncited"><div>The DMR system is very critical, and with a small frequency deviation, this is possible. Use an SDR to adjust the frequency on the Baofeng.<br>I'm assuming you're using the original Baofeng antenna. If you use an external base antenna, the Baofeng could saturate, causing this error.</div></blockquote>Thanks for taking the time to reply, EA3V. The first thing I did when I noticed the reception problem with OpenGD77 was use the firmware's calibration tool to confirm that the radio was on frequency. Also, when I returned from OpenGD77 to factory firmware, DMR reception improved without making any other changes, including frequency calibration.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=914">w9lw</a> — Wed Apr 16, 2025 2:00 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
